<title>GERMANY: German IBIS share system to be replaced by end-97.</title>
<headline>German IBIS share system to be replaced by end-97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German bourse said on Tuesday that it would close its IBIS electronic trading system at the end of 1997 since its new electronic trading system will then be in operation.</p>
<p>The bourse said the new &quot;front-end&quot; for electronic trading will be put into operation in the 1997 second quarter and the &quot;back-end&quot; of the system will be in operation during the 1997 fourth quarter, allowing the IBIS system to be shut.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
